{"id":"e24332c1-7f01-4bbe-bb71-5e61050cbfd6","object":"chat.completion","created":1784987490,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('case must be a dict')\\n    if 'text' not in case or 'passes' not in case or 'max_rounds' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('Missing required fields: text, passes, max_rounds')\\n    text = str(case['text'])\\n    passes = case['passes']\\n    if not isinstance(passes, list):\\n        raise ValueError('passes must be a list')\\n    max_rounds = int(case['max_rounds'])\\n    if max_rounds <= 0:\\n        raise ValueError('max_rounds must be positive')\\n    applications = []\\n    for round_num in range(max_rounds):\\n        changed_in_round = False\\n        for p in passes:\\n            if not isinstance(p, dict):\\n                raise ValueError('each pass must be a dict')\\n            name = p.get('name')\\n            old = p.get('old')\\n            new = p.get('new')\\n            if not all(isinstance(x, str) for x in (name, old, new)):\\n                raise ValueError('pass name, old, new must be strings')\\n            if old in text:\\n                text = text.replace(old, new, 1)\\n                applications.append(name)\\n                changed_in_round = True\\n        if not changed_in_round:\\n            return {\\n                'applications': applications,\\n                'fixed_point': True,\\n                'text': text\\n            }\\n    return {\\n        'applications': applications,\\n        'fixed_point': False,\\n        'text': text\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) that processes the given payload. The task is \"pass_scheduler_fixed_point\". Based on the description and the example payload, we have a text, passes (list of objects with old/new), max_rounds. We need to repeatedly apply passes in order, each pass does at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep (meaning per pass, find first occurrence of old string in current text and replace with new? But \"eligible rewrite\" might mean only the first occurrence? Actually description: \"Each pass performs at most its first eligible rewrite per sweep.\" And \"Apply passes in their registered order.\" \"Repeat full sweeps until none changes or the round budget is consumed.\" \"Record only passes that change the artifact.\" Return \"text\" (final artifact), \"applications\" (list of pass names that changed something, in order of application?), and \"fixed_point\" (boolean indicating if termination was due to no changes or budget? Probably True if no changes in last sweep, False if max_rounds reached? But need to check schema: fixed_point is boolean. The description says \"fixed-point flag\". Likely True if we reached a fixed point (no changes in a full sweep) before running out of rounds; False if we stopped due to max_rounds. But careful: also restart policy? Not clear. However given the payload, there's no restart_policy etc. The candidate_artifact mentions \"restart_policy\", \"cache_semantics\", \"interestingness_preserved\". But the payload only has text, passes, max_rounds. Possibly those are part of the case but not in this fixture? The fixture only shows these fields. But we must use only fields present in the payload. So we ignore missing fields. Also \"interestingness_preserved\" might be a required check? Not in payload. So we just implement the core algorithm.\n\nInterpretation: We have a string text. Passes are ordered list of transformation rules: each has name, old, new. For each sweep, we go through passes in order. For each pass, we look for the first occurrence of old in the current text. If found, we replace only that first occurrence with new (i.e., at most one replacement per pass per sweep). If replacement occurred, we record the pass name in applications list (order of application)